installation :thorong_cold_house do
  name "The Thorong Cold House"
  tags :water, :ecology, :biotech, :catastrophe
  prominence :marginal

  prose <<~PROSE
    One unheated dry-stone room on the Thorong pass at 5,400 metres, four days' carry above the intakes it serves, where a candidate for #{ref :the_catchment_list, "a catchment list"} is shown the winter its ender line claims will stop it. North door, slate roof, a stone bench and two racks. No power, no instrument, no lock beyond a hasp and a stone.

    Nobody winters with it. The door is closed at the first snow and opened at the melt, and the carry up and the carry down are what the house costs.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :mechanics, heading: "The Set And The Melt Carry"
    A candidate goes up as a sealed set of twenty glass tubes in a padded case: ten holding the organism on its own substrate, five holding it with the compound its requirement line names, five holding substrate alone. The tubes are racked off the floor, spaced a hand apart, and their positions are drawn on the case lid before the door closes.

    An entry survives the winter if the five withheld tubes come down clean. Growth in a withheld tube means the requirement line is wrong. Growth across all fifteen means the ender line is wrong as well, and the entry does not stand.

    A set that thaws on the way down reads as nothing, so the melt carry goes in one push through the night, and a carrier who has to shelter opens the case and abandons the set rather than bringing a warm one to the bench. #{ref :the_thorong_book, "The house's book"} records nine abandoned sets against forty-one read.

    One rack position every autumn is held for a set nobody above the pass has an interest in: a #{ref :gate_moss, "gate-moss"} set off a crossing bed, read first at the melt, against which that winter is severe or mild. Without it the year's other readings compare to nothing.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :people, heading: "Who Carries"
    The carry is contracted by the season out of the villages below the pass, and the same families have taken the Thorong sets up since the house was built. Machines are not used above the last shelter: autonomous carriers lose navigation on the pass, and a fungal courier cannot be sent into a catchment whose list it is not on.

    A carrier is paid on delivery of a cold case and paid again for an abandoned one, at the same rate, on the carrier's word alone. #{ref :the_overwintered_set, "The Overwintered Set"} came down this pass in one night in the melt of 2089.

    Some of the carries are paid for from outside the Holds. The #{ref :the_gatekeepers, "Gatekeepers"} send sealed sets up for #{ref :the_season_credit, "a credit"} against their own four-day work and pay the same villages the same rate, abandoned sets included. A foreign set travels alone in its case and no monastery's candidates ride with it. That is the whole of the arrangement, and it is renegotiated every autumn by whoever is contracting the carry.
  PROSE

  log "2026-08-09 — The set is ten organism tubes, five with the named requirement withheld and five substrate blanks, from containment screening practice where an engineered dependency is tested by withholding the compound it is supposed to require and reading against blanks. That decided what a failed reading means here: a clean withheld tube proves the dependency, and growth in one proves the entry's requirement line was written wrong rather than that the organism changed."
end
